comment.body:
Please validate the sort URL param before storing it as typed state. With the new custom radio UI, an unknown value leaves the radiogroup with no checked option and can leak arbitrary strings into the search hook/fallback NIP-50 query; invalid values should canonicalize back to the default Hot sort.

```suggestion
  const [sortMode, setSortMode] = useState<SortMode | 'relevance'>(() => {
    const sortParam = searchParams.get('sort');

    return SORT_MODES.some(mode => mode.value === sortParam)
      ? (sortParam as SortMode | 'relevance')
      : 'hot';
  });
```

